      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A stoichiometric amount of tetrachlorocatechol (4 equiv, 2.08 × 10^{-4} mol) was deprotonated with 2 equiv of triethylamine per equivalent of ligand in methanol (3 mL) and added dropwise to a solution of Y(NO3)3·xH2O (2 equiv, 1.04 × 10^{-4} mol) in methanol (2 mL). The solution was left to stand at room temperature in the dark. Amorphous solid that formed was removed by filtration daily; after no more precipitate was evident the solution was left to evaporate. After about 2 weeks, crystals of 1-Cl could be selected from a mixture of 2-Cl, 3-Cl, and amorphous material. Crystallographic samples were kept in contact with the mother liquor. Isolated yttrium compounds decompose after a day or two in air.",
